    "mitigation": "Reject zero-duration configurations for every mode that relies on a pool TWAP or TWAP verification, and enforce a protocol-defined minimum observation period. Do not use the same current spot price both as the effective collateral-price source and as its verification source. Require an independent, fresh oracle source or an independent nonzero-duration TWAP with explicit deviation, liquidity, and observation-history checks. The configuration should also prevent a collateral position pool from serving as its own valuation reference where practical.",
